VALUES ('NTRS','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for asset servicing, custody, wealth management, asset management, fund administration, and institutional banking can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Losses, volatility, collateral changes, or funding stress can impair capital. Capital rules, fiduciary duties, market structure, or misconduct can change economics. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','NTRS SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0000073124&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides NORTHERN TRUST CORP''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
