VALUES ('ORCL','owner_summary','editorial_analysis','Oracle is using its durable database, applications, and support franchise to finance a much more capital-intensive AI cloud expansion. The ownership question is whether rapidly growing OCI demand and a $638 billion remaining performance obligation can produce returns above the cost of data centers, debt, leases, and potential equity dilution.','Defines the central ownership lens and its falsifiable operating variables.','Oracle 2026 Form 10-K','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1341439/000119312526277521/orcl-20260531.htm','The annual filing reports Oracle’s cloud and software mix, revenue, operating cash flow, capital expenditures, cash, debt, property and equipment, lease commitments, revenue recognition, competition, customers, infrastructure obligations, and risk factors.','2026-06-22','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
