VALUES ('ORCL','revenue_model','editorial_analysis','Cloud arrangements generally run one to five years and are recognized ratably or as usage occurs. Software support is primarily recurring, licenses are generally recognized when control transfers, and hardware and services are recognized as products and work are delivered.','Explains how reported activity converts into revenue and owner economics.','Oracle 2026 Form 10-K','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1341439/000119312526277521/orcl-20260531.htm','The annual filing reports Oracle’s cloud and software mix, revenue, operating cash flow, capital expenditures, cash, debt, property and equipment, lease commitments, revenue recognition, competition, customers, infrastructure obligations, and risk factors.','2026-06-22','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
