VALUES ('ORCL','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Fiscal 2026 capital expenditures of $55.66 billion exceeded operating cash flow by $23.69 billion, and management expects the infrastructure program to require additional debt and equity financing. Current and long-term debt reached $129.54 billion, fiscal 2026 interest expense was $4.60 billion, and roughly $260 billion of additional lease commitments had not yet commenced at year end. RPO is not recognized revenue and depends on Oracle delivering capacity, customers performing under contracts, service availability, pricing, utilization, and the economics of each arrangement. AWS, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud, enterprise-software competitors, customer-built systems, and open-source technologies compete for workloads while Oracle’s fiscal 2026 software revenue declined 1%.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','Oracle 2026 Form 10-K','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1341439/000119312526277521/orcl-20260531.htm','The annual filing reports Oracle’s cloud and software mix, revenue, operating cash flow, capital expenditures, cash, debt, property and equipment, lease commitments, revenue recognition, competition, customers, infrastructure obligations, and risk factors.','2026-06-22','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
