VALUES ('RCL','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Ships require long lead times, large progress payments, ongoing maintenance, and high utilization; supply cannot be adjusted quickly when demand changes. Geopolitics, recession, fuel, weather, illness, incidents, port restrictions, or negative publicity can disrupt itineraries and booking behavior. Newbuilds, destination projects, debt service, dividends, and repurchases compete for cash, making capital-allocation discipline central to per-share returns.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','Royal Caribbean 2025 Form 10-K','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/884887/000088488726000007/rcl-20251231.htm','The annual filing describes Royal Caribbean, Celebrity, Silversea, TUI Cruises, the combined fleet, passenger-ticket and onboard revenue, capacity and yield metrics, ship commitments, debt, competition, regulation, and operating risks.','2026-02-11','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
