VALUES ('REG','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for grocery-anchored shopping centers, leasing, development, redevelopment, mixed-use projects, and necessity retail can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Vacancy, churn, customer consolidation, or property obsolescence can reduce cash flow. Leverage and maturities expose owners to rates and capital-market availability. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','REG SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0000910606&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides REGENCY CENTERS REIT CORP''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
