INSERT INTO company_dossiers (ticker,status,description,lede,sells,revenue_model,opportunity,must_go_right,editor_note,bull_title,bull_json,bear_title,bear_json,thesis_breaker,financial_drivers_json,risks_json,monitor_json,questions_json,competitors,evidence_date,validated_at,published_at,updated_at) VALUES ('MKC','published','MCCORMICK & CO NON-VOTING INC operates in consumer staples, focused on spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution.','MCCORMICK & CO NON-VOTING INC gives owners exposure to spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution. The central question is whether its competitive position and reinvestment can convert demand into durable per-share cash generation after the full cost of capital, execution, and industry risk.','MCCORMICK & CO NON-VOTING INC provides spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution to consumers, retailers, distributors, restaurants, and food-service or institutional channels. Owners should verify segment mix, customer concentration, contract terms, and geographic exposure in the latest Form 10-K and 10-Q.','Branded consumable product sales through retail, wholesale, direct, and food-service channels, net of promotions and trade spending.','Brand strength, distribution, innovation, premiumization, and international penetration can support recurring demand and pricing. For MCCORMICK & CO NON-VOTING INC, the owner must test whether spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution can gain profitable share rather than treating addressable-market growth as company value by itself.','Volume must remain resilient after pricing, innovation must offset category maturity, input costs must be managed, and marketing must sustain consumer relevance.','This owner brief uses the issuer''s SEC filing history, earnings-related 8-K record, proxy disclosures, and official company materials as its evidence spine. Bull and bear points are hypotheses to verify against the latest reported segment, cash-flow, balance-sheet, and management-commentary evidence—not recommendations or price targets.','What the filing and call evidence could support','["MCCORMICK & CO NON-VOTING INC''s position in spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution can compound value if demand converts into durable share, pricing, and cash rather than temporary volume.","Habit, brand trust, shelf space, route-to-market scale, supply chain, and marketing can support durable category positions.","Operating leverage and disciplined reinvestment can expand per-share free cash flow when revenue quality, margins, and capital intensity improve together.","Official filings and earnings materials create a quarterly scorecard for testing management''s claims against delivered results and cash conversion."]','What owners must be prepared to disprove','["Demand for spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow.","Pricing, private label, health preferences, or weak innovation can reduce units.","Commodity, packaging, labor, weather, or logistics can pressure availability and margin.","Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash."]','The owner thesis breaks if MCCORMICK & CO NON-VOTING INC cannot defend its position in spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution and repeatedly fails to convert reported growth into resilient per-share free cash flow after required investment, balance-sheet obligations, and dilution.','[{"label":"ORGANIC SALES","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"volume, price, mix, geography, categories, and share"},{"label":"GROSS MARGIN","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"commodities, packaging, labor, freight, productivity, and promotion"},{"label":"BRAND & CASH","value":"Quarterly filing scorecard","detail":"marketing, innovation, working capital, capex, dividends, and free cash flow"},{"label":"REVENUE QUALITY","value":"Growth versus durability","detail":"Separate price, volume, mix, acquisitions, foreign exchange, backlog, and one-time items; reconcile growth with retention and cash collection."},{"label":"BALANCE SHEET","value":"Resilience and optionality","detail":"Track cash, debt, leases, pensions, commitments, covenants, refinancing needs, and contingent liabilities disclosed in the latest filing."},{"label":"PER-SHARE VALUE","value":"Owner cash conversion","detail":"Reconcile net income with operating cash, capex, acquisitions, dividends, repurchases, stock compensation, and diluted share count."}]','[{"title":"Volume and elasticity","level":"High","text":"Pricing, private label, health preferences, or weak innovation can reduce units.","signal":"Organic volume, share, household penetration, and promotion"},{"title":"Input and supply chain","level":"High","text":"Commodity, packaging, labor, weather, or logistics can pressure availability and margin.","signal":"Gross margin, service levels, spot prices, and inventory"},{"title":"Retailer and regulation","level":"High","text":"Concentrated retailers or health, labeling, tax, and environmental rules can alter economics.","signal":"Customer concentration, shelf position, new rules, and reformulation cost"},{"title":"Capital allocation","level":"Medium","text":"Acquisitions, internal investment, debt, dividends, and repurchases can create or destroy per-share value.","signal":"Return on invested capital, impairments, leverage, share count, and post-investment cash generation"},{"title":"Reporting, legal, and governance","level":"Medium","text":"Controls, estimates, litigation, tax, incentives, or governance choices can alter reported economics and owner outcomes.","signal":"Restatements, control weaknesses, estimate changes, proceedings, proxy incentives, and related-party disclosures"}]','[{"title":"Latest 10-Q versus prior expectations","text":"Compare reported operating drivers, cash conversion, balance-sheet changes, and risk language with the prior quarter and owner thesis.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Management commentary versus delivery","text":"Record the measurable commitments made in the latest official earnings materials and test them against subsequent filings.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Downside leading indicators","text":"Watch Organic volume, share, household penetration, and promotion; Gross margin, service levels, spot prices, and inventory; Customer concentration, shelf position, new rules, and reformulation cost.","impact":"BEAR CASE"},{"title":"Per-share capital allocation","text":"Measure whether retained cash, acquisitions, debt reduction, dividends, and repurchases improve durable value per diluted share.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}]','["Which disclosed operating metric best proves that MCCORMICK & CO NON-VOTING INC is strengthening its position in spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution?","What changed in the latest 10-Q relative to the preceding 10-K and management''s prior commentary?","Which portion of reported growth is recurring, contractual, or repeatable, and which portion is cyclical or one-time?","What balance-sheet or off-balance-sheet obligation matters most in a downside case?","Does management''s compensation framework reward per-share owner value or primarily scale and adjusted metrics?","What measurable development would invalidate the thesis rather than merely create short-term price volatility?"]','MCCORMICK & CO NON-VOTING INC competes with public and private operators across spices, seasonings, condiments, flavor solutions, consumer brands, foodservice, and global ingredient distribution; the comparable set below is a research starting point and must be normalized for business mix, leverage, accounting, and capital intensity.','2026-08-02',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP) ON CONFLICT(ticker) DO UPDATE SET status='published',description=excluded.description,lede=excluded.lede,sells=excluded.sells,revenue_model=excluded.revenue_model,opportunity=excluded.opportunity,must_go_right=excluded.must_go_right,editor_note=excluded.editor_note,bull_title=excluded.bull_title,bull_json=excluded.bull_json,bear_title=excluded.bear_title,bear_json=excluded.bear_json,thesis_breaker=excluded.thesis_breaker,financial_drivers_json=excluded.financial_drivers_json,risks_json=excluded.risks_json,monitor_json=excluded.monitor_json,questions_json=excluded.questions_json,competitors=excluded.competitors,evidence_date=excluded.evidence_date,validated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,published_at=COALESCE(company_dossiers.published_at,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
